[statement]
A `!` entry whose operator admits earlier versions forbids a package
providing the name at no version: `app` states `!v<3`, `a` provides `v`
at no version, and asked for both, apk refuses. With `!v>1`, apk installs
both.

[repository]
P:app
V:1
D:!v<3

P:a
V:1
p:v

[request]
app
a

[answer apk-tools 3.0.9-r0]
| ERROR: unable to select packages:
|   a-1:
|     breaks: app-1[!v<3]
|     satisfies: world[a]
refused
